<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1967</h1><p class="ref-lede">1967 in world history: 37 events, 8 births, 21 deaths, 1 work, 3 states founded and 5 that came to an end. 305 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1963">1963</a><a href="/years/1964">1964</a><a href="/years/1965">1965</a><a href="/years/1966">1966</a><a href="/years/1967" aria-current="page">1967</a><a href="/years/1968">1968</a><a href="/years/1969">1969</a><a href="/years/1970">1970</a><a href="/years/1971">1971</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-27">27 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Outer Space Treaty signed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> signed a treaty barring nuclear weapons from orbit and forbidding any nation from claiming the Moon or other celestial bodies. It remains the basis of space law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-27">27 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fire kills three Apollo 1 astronauts during a test</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A flash fire in the pure-oxygen cabin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 1 killed Gus Grissom, Ed White and Roger Chaffee during a launch rehearsal at Cape Kennedy. NASA redesigned the spacecraft before flying again.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-27">27 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Australians vote to include Aboriginal people in the census</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Over 90 per cent voted to count Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people in the population and to let the Commonwealth make laws for them. It remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s most successful referendum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-30">30 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Biafra declares independence from Nigeria</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel Odumegwu Ojukwu proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biafra">Biafra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s south-east. The civil war that followed lasted until 1970, and up to two million people died, many from famine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-5">5 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Israel launches the Six-Day War</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Israeli air strikes destroyed most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s air force on the ground. In six days Israel took Sinai, Gaza, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-10">10 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Six-Day War ends in a ceasefire</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fighting ended with Israel holding Sinai, Gaza, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a>, East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a>. The status of these territories has remained central to the conflict ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-3">3 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sweden switches to driving on the right</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At 4.50 am all traffic in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> stopped, changed sides and restarted on the right. Dagen H, 'H Day', went smoothly after years of preparation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-8">8 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Che Guevara is captured in Bolivia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolivian troops, aided by the CIA, wounded and captured Ernesto 'Che' Guevara in the Yuro ravine. He was executed the next day at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-higuera">La Higuera</a>, and his image became an enduring icon of revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-10">10 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Outer Space Treaty enters into force</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Outer Space Treaty came into effect, forming the basis of international space law. It bars nuclear weapons from orbit and forbids any nation from claiming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the Moon or other celestial bodies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-3">3 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Christiaan Barnard performs the first human heart transplant</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Groote Schuur Hospital in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a>, Christiaan Barnard's team transplanted a heart into Louis Washkansky. He lived for 18 days before dying of pneumonia, but the operation launched transplant surgery.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tlatelolco">Treaty of Tlatelolco</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Tlatelolco, signed in Mexico City on 14 February 1967, created a nuclear-weapon-free zone in Latin America and the Caribbean, the first in a populated region.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/samlaut-uprising">Samlaut uprising</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Samlaut uprising was a peasant revolt that broke out in 1967 around Samlaut in Battambang province, Cambodia, provoked by forced government rice purchases and land grievances.</p></div></li></ol></section>
