<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/commonwealth-of-australia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Commonwealth%20of%20Australia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Commonwealth of Australia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum allows Aboriginal people to be counted in the census</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Greece.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Greece</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The colonels’ coup; Constantine II goes into exile after a failed counter-coup</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-yemen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20Yemen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South Yemen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain withdraws and the People’s Republic of South Yemen is proclaimed on 30 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Buganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Buganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Uganda’s new constitution abolishes the kingdoms</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Ankole.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Ankole</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Uganda's new constitution abolishes the kingdom</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bunyoro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bunyoro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The monarchy is abolished; it is restored as a cultural institution in 1993</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/uganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Uganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Uganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A republican constitution abolishes the kingdoms</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Arusha Declaration launches ujamaa socialism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/swahili"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swahili.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swahili</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Tanzania makes Swahili the language of government and of primary schooling</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/military-junta"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Military%20junta.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Military junta</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Colonels seize power in Greece and rule until their coup in Cyprus brings their fall in 1974</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/syrian-arab-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syrian%20Arab%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syrian Arab Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the Six-Day War Israel captures two-thirds of the Golan Heights in under 48 hours.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the Six-Day War Israel captures the Sinai Peninsula and the Gaza Strip; an Emergency Law expanding police powers is enacted and stays in force until 2012.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Singapore co-founds the Association of Southeast Asian Nations and begins interchanging its dollar at par with Brunei's.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/aboriginal-australians"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Aboriginal%20Australians.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Aboriginal Australians</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A referendum passed by a 90% majority gives Aboriginal affairs to the federal government and removes discriminatory census provisions from the Constitution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/maoism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Maoism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Maoism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Naxalbari uprising in India begins the Naxalite movement, which spreads Quotations from Chairman Mao Zedong</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Israel’s victory in the Six-Day War damages pan-Arabism’s credibility</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A new constitution creates a bicameral legislature, and Nguyễn Văn Thiệu is elected president with 34% of the vote in a widely criticised poll</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/jerusalem"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jerusalem.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jerusalem</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Israel takes East Jerusalem in the Six-Day War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/sigiriya"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sigiriya.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sigiriya</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Paint was splashed on the frescoes in an act of vandalism, and restoration lasted until April 1968</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/prague-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prague%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prague Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At the Writers' Congress in June, Ludvík Vaculík, Milan Kundera and Antonín Liehm deliver speeches against the regime's control of literature</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/populism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Populism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Populism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A conference at the London School of Economics fails to produce a unified theory of populism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/african-socialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/African%20socialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>African socialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Julius Nyerere issues the Arusha Declaration, committing Tanzania to a socialist reform programme built on Ujamaa</span></li></ul></section>
